      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#0 · Taylor's Antikythera image; Freeth et al. 2006 (paraphrased abstract)",
          "title": "The sky exceeds the hand which makes it readable",
          "italic": "The instrument embodies attunement: exactness in the means by which a finite instrument answers to a wider field — the world continues beyond the attention.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "An observer approaches a situated dial: a small material arrangement can place celestial relations before someone whose life has to proceed among them. Sun, Moon, calendar, eclipse, instrument and reader acquire relations through a work of coordination which preserves their different offices. The whole begins in this disproportion: a person cannot bring the heavens to the scale of a hand by",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "possessing them; craft can give the hand a determinate relation to their movements. Freeth and colleagues' 2006 abstract places the Greek device around the end of the second century BCE, with lunar phases, a luni-solar calendar and eclipse prediction among its reported functions; Antikythera is the find-place of the shipwreck. No ancient owner, commission or act of consultation is invented.\n\nOccurrences: Sun, Moon, calendar, eclipse indications (#0); the smallness productive of use (#0); the shipwreck find-place (#0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
