      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · the distributed source of intelligibility",
          "title": "Gearing gives differentiated movement a transmissible body",
          "italic": "The mechanism demonstrates that relations must be carried by something that can actually move, fit and indicate — without becoming the celestial event itself.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "One part moves in relation to another because the material arrangement constrains their relation. A scale makes that movement readable; an inscription tells a reader what a mark is to be read as. The source of intelligibility stays distributed: gear, referent, convention, question. Remove the relation among these offices and the",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "completeness of one part cannot compensate — a wheel can turn correctly while its indication is misread; an inscription can remain legible when the motion it describes is missing. The observer remains an active term: a display answers a question only through a reading, and the reader stands within the heavens whose relations the device helps disclose.\n\nOccurrences: gears, scale, inscription (#1); the misread indication (#1); the reader within the read world (#1).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
