      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · the Metonic and Antikythera matheme; A16 return",
          "title": "Coordinated cycles keep their differences",
          "italic": "A material ratio can be exact as an arrangement while its astronomical fit retains a residual — the mytheme carries the lived consequence of reckoning inside a changing world.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Several cycles become mutually readable while keeping the differences which made coordination necessary. A lunar indication, a date and an eclipse indication answer different questions even when consulted together. The matheme distinguishes the chosen calendar count from the approximate natural periods it relates, and the Metonic from the Saros operation. Attunement therefore includes the possibility of discrepancy: a",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "reader who recognises what an indication does and where its warrant ends can use the instrument more exactly. The obligation sharpens when the image models knowledge itself: if an answer excludes the circumstance under which it was obtained, greater confidence in its execution can make the exclusion harder to perceive. A16 receives the differential field in which the situated dial coordinates heterogeneous positions.\n\nOccurrences: calendar and eclipse indications (#0, #2); the Metonic/Saros distinction (#2); the residual (#2); the excluded circumstance warning (#2).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
