      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#3 · Freeth et al. 2006 recovery; 2021 model, q001 p.2 and q002 p.12",
          "title": "The damaged instrument makes answerability unavoidable",
          "italic": "The reconstruction demonstrates rigour precisely by naming what remains unavailable — model coherence and fit support the proposal without removing the limit.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Modern investigators encounter an achieved work through surviving parts; the relation runs from fragment toward the arrangement which could have given it office. Absent parts are consequential: filling their places is reasoning whose warrant must stay distinguishable from the evidence that prompted it. The 2021 study proposes a front display of nine outputs — Moon, Nodes, Mercury, Venus, Sun, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Date — carried by",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "nested tubes and arms; and its conclusion retains the decisive limit: lost evidence prevents the authors from claiming a replica of the original. The 2006 recovery is not retrospectively credited with every later feature; the model is not an intact recovered machine. The aftermath belongs to the whole image: what was made becomes a damaged inheritance; what is recovered becomes a model; the model changes the questions that can next be asked.\n\nOccurrences: the wreck and surviving fragments (#0, #3); the nine-output proposal (#3); the no-replica limit (#3); the reverse direction of reconstruction (#3).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
